; Handler of the word HELP
;
; For the player (a hint is never given to an order for someone else; those
; skip to the next word) prints the hint for the player's location from
; HintTable ("A trolls door needs a trolls key." in the trolls path,
; for instance), or "You're doing fine." when the location has no hint. Prints
; in the input window (RawOutputFlag = 1). Then returns to the dispatcher
; (#R$82B3).
; .
; Hardware: none.
@label=WordHelp
c$83A0 LD A,($B6EA)         ; actor
 $83A3 AND A
 $83A4 JP NZ,$75B4          ; not the player: next word
 $83A7 PUSH HL
 $83A8 PUSH IX
 $83AA LD HL,$B467          ; "You're doing fine."
 $83AD LD A,($C12B)         ; player location (first byte of its location list)
 $83B0 LD IX,$83CD
 $83B4 CALL $9DBD           ; find the hint
 $83B7 JR Z,$83BF           ; none: keep the default
 $83B9 LD L,(IX+$01)
 $83BC LD H,(IX+$02)
@label=WordHelp_Print
*$83BF LD A,$01             ; RawOutputFlag: input window
@isub=LD (RawOutputFlag),A
 $83C1 LD ($B701),A
 $83C4 CALL $72DD
 $83C7 POP IX
 $83C9 POP HL
 $83CA JP $82B3
